WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:11.000
Hi, welcome back to the at-home Lam Rim retreat.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:23.680
We've reached session number 15.
The name of this session is "Arming the Bomb."

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:37.520
And the picture I chose is somebody
turning on a landmine.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.920
So they carry those landmines around,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:51.160
they are not armed, they are not turned on.
Then they put them underground.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.040
They turn it on and they hide it.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.440
So we are talking about a karmic seed.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:10.160
At link number two, that seed was planted
in the consciousness.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:20.040
It's like first putting a watermelon seed
under the ground.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:33.920
I didn't grow up gardening. I thought Xīguā, watermelon, were grown in the store.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.240
Then I spent more time with Veronica--
she loves gardening--

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:53.280
and so I got more aware of how plants are grown.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.120
Right now in Arizona, it's March--

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.760
we just bought our watermelon seeds

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:13.160
and in the next week or two
we will put them in the ground.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:19.640
So you put them in the ground
and then you cover it with dirt.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:26.680
That's like the karmic seed planted at link number two.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:36.520
The guy is making the pots.
Now, I think it's a fascinating thing,

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:47.040
For the first two or three weeks
that seed will sit there underground.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:03:01.160
Now if you put that seed in your drawer, in your desk,
it can sit there for a long, long time.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.840
For two or three years... it's not going to open.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.920
But if you put it underground
and you start watering  and you start fertilizing,

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:19.040
something in this seed wakes up.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.240
And in my mind I always picture it like this...

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:34.120
the water comes down through the soil,
the water touches the seed,

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:45.080
and it starts to seep into the seed and the water wakes up all the factory workers inside the seed.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:54.000
And they're like "Water, water! It's time,
they got the water!

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.160
Okay, let's get this watermelon plant going!"

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.760
They all start running around the seed,

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:08.280
like a factory, and it wakes the seed up.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:16.000
And then two or three weeks later
the seed actually gets fatter,

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:24.080
it's almost like a balloon.
And then, it's like you pop a balloon,

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:29.520
and then "boom," this first sprout comes out.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:39.720
And it grows for three four months
and then you get watermelons.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:45.000
And by the way, if you want to go deeper,

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:54.040
Arya Nagarjuna--sometimes he is called "The Arya,"

00:04:55.040 --> 00:05:04.440
which means "the coolest guy who saw emptiness directly."

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:12.000
I'll just throw a little bit of seed in your mind.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:20.040
Nagarjuna would say that
the water never touches the seed.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:30.040
So how can that seed grow then?
Well to learn the answer to that,

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:42.080
you're going to have to come and look at
our special video series about Nagarjuna.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:48.120
We are translating his greatest book.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:54.040
It's a commentary by the greatest Tibetan
lama of all time, Choney Lama.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:04.600
Almost the greatest.
Except for my lama and Tsongkapa.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:09.680
But we're going to be talking about that
in our special Nagarjuna class.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:21.000
Okay, let's go back.
That seed was put under the ground in link number two.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:31.200
The seed was planted in your mind and it
sat there under the ground,

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:39.080
and something--water and fertilizer--came down and touched it.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:50.120
And because of the water and the fertilizer, the seed started get fat, fat, fat, fat, fat.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:56.440
Then it was ready to split open and make a sprout.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:02.240
So now the question comes,

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:09.040
What is the power or force which is like
fertilizer or water for a mental seed?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.920
What makes the seed wake...

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:30.760
... what makes the factory workers inside the mental seed wake up and start working to push out the sprout?

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:40.640
Now there are two links, number eight and number nine--

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:49.680
technically they are called "beginning desire"
and then "advanced desire.".

00:07:55.520 --> 00:08:05.840
They are the force which makes the
seed factory workers start running around
and working to push the sprout out.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:18.200
So I have a special strategy for these two.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.520
I'm gonna read the text to you,

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:31.240
you can see the lower school idea

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:43.120
about what wakes up the seed,
or what makes the seed fat.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.480
And then when we finish the text,

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:55.160
I'm going to take you into
a more advanced understanding

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:00.840
of what makes this seed fat and strong.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:06.680
First we're going to start with link number eight.

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:17.160
"Beginning desire," "initial desire," and the picture is a... it's a terrible painting, I'm sorry...

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:24.680
but it's a big fat man, not a lady,
having a feast. Overeating.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:44.000
And this Fēicháng pàng (非常胖), this fat guy, what does he represent?

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:49.480
gyepa sepa (BRGYAD PA SRED PA) means "link number eight is called beginning desire."

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:56.920
And the lower school explanation,

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:04.640
you get different kinds of desire that start in your heart.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:11.280
Here's one:
tsorwa dewa la mindrelwar dupay sepa (TSOR BA BDE BA LA MI 'BRAL BAR 'DOD PA'I SRED PA)

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:22.000
means "you feel this desire that you don't want to lose the things that felt good to you" in link number seven.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.080
Or there's another version of this desire.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:42.640
dukgnelwa la drel du kyi sepa (SDUG BSNGAL BA LA 'BRAL 'DOD KYI SRED PA) means "you do want to get away

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:49.080
from something that was painful"
during link number seven.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.160
So you have
drelwar shenpa ('BRAL BAR ZHEN PA).
drelwar shenpa means you get a strong desire

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:04.520
that you either don't want to,
or you do want to get away from that thing.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:16.320
tang nyom la mi nyampay chir du sepa yin
(BTANG SNYOMS LA MI NYAMS PA'I PHYIR DU SRED PA YIN).

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:23.120
tang nyom la (BTANG SNYOMS LA)--
you can also have a neutral feeling

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:30.920
and you can have a hope that it's going to go on.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.800
So that would be another kind of desire.

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.000
tsorway kyen gyi sepa kyewar shepa ni
(TSOR BA'I RKYEN GYIS SRED PA
SKYE BAR BSHAD PA NI)--

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:53.440
when we say that the link number seven
of feeling has triggered desire at link number eight--beginning desire...

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:05.200
when we say that number seven, feeling,
is triggering desire,

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:17.480
gong (DGONGS) in the next sentence means "what we're really saying." gong-- "the real thought."

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.040
saṃdhi-nirmocana

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:32.120
We're talking about feelings that have
been triggered by number six,

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:41.120
which is contact with the outside world.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:46.400
But we're talking about special
kind of contact with the outside world,

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:53.840
which is mixed up with misunderstanding.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:59.480
The wife has eyes when she comes in the kitchen,

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:06.760
then she opens her eyes and she kind of opens her ears,

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:13.880
and then there's the red face of the husband
and the yelling "You're stupid!"

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:21.400
And her mind makes contact with those
sounds and those shapes.

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:30.120
But that contact with his red face and his loud words,

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:38.880
it's mixed up with misunderstanding
where he's coming from.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:45.880
Can you hear your husband calling you stupid?

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:51.960
"Yeah, I hear." What's the feeling in the back of your mind?

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:56.560
"I didn't do anything and he's yelling at me."

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:06.800
And in that case, the contact with the red face
and the contact with the loud words
is mixed up with misunderstanding.

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:18.200
And if that contact creates a feeling of anger

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:26.520
and that anger creates a desire
at link number eight to get out of the kitchen,

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:31.480
divorce this guy,

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:44.880
then we have bad karmas
and dirty good karmas getting woken up.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:58.720
But he says marikpa me na (MA RIG PA MED NA)--
if the wife at that moment says,
"he's yelling at me because I yelled at my kids,"

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:08.320
she's still going to have feeling,

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:18.880
but she's not going to have this
link number eight desire to get away.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:30.520
And that's a subtle thing we have to talk about it--it doesn't mean she doesn't want to get out of the kitchen.

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:36.120
It means she wants to stop it,
but she understands how to stop it.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:44.840
Don't forget I'm still kind of keeping to the lower school.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:57.080
Okay, link number nine.
The picture is a monkey grabbing a fruit.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.400
And here's the definition of it:

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:10.320
gupa lenpa ni, sepa je cher pelwe
(DGU PA LEN PA NI, SRED PA JE CHER 'PHEL BAS)--
at link number nine, which is called "advanced desire,"

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:18.200
your desire gets stronger and stronger,

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:27.040
yul la dun ching chakpa te (YUL LA 'DUN CING CHAGS PA STE),
and then you get a special craving for the object

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:38.160
and that craving can come in four different kinds.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:45.240
Generally. Not as this link, okay, generally.

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:55.960
He should have said that,
and a lot of the texts on the twelve links...

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:08.920
...they start discussing the divisions of desire in general, but not link number nine desire.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:21.400
So it can be a little bit confusing.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:27.160
So in general, here's four kinds of desire.

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:41.080
dupa nyewar lenpa ni du yun la chakpa
('DOD PA NYE BAR LEN PA NI 'DOD YON LA CHAGS PA)--
one is called "desire for desirable things."

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:53.240
And that's called du yun la chakpa ('DOD YON LA CHAGS PA).
du yun la chakpa means
"attraction to beautiful things,"

00:17:56.800 --> 00:18:04.600
like nice clothes, tasty food, or the feeling of sex.

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:10.920
These are all kinds of attraction to the objects of desire.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:23.120
Then there's tawa nyewar lenpa (LTA BA NYE BAR LEN PA),
which means "desire for thinking of things a certain way,"
"desire for certain viewpoints."

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:39.320
And this is described as ta ngen la chakpa (LTA NGAN LA CHAGS PA)-- "attachment to negative... wrong viewpoints."

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.120
"Bad viewpoints."

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:52.800
Like, "Oh hey, there's no karma. You can do what you want."

00:18:53.720 --> 00:19:03.880
So that's a viewpoint, and it's completely wrong,
but you can get attached to it, like alcoholism.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:13.040
So the second kind of advanced desire in this list

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:20.240
is an attraction to mistaken ideas.

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:29.640
Except a special one and we're saving that one for later.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:35.080
That one is "wrong idea about me."

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:42.640
That's coming later. Okay number three.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:49.160
tsultrim dang tul shuk nyewar lenpa ni ta ngen dang dreway tsultrim dang trul shuk menpa la chakpa
TSUL KHRIMS DANG BRTUL ZHUGS NYE BAR LEN PA NI LTA NGAN DANG 'BREL BA'I TSUL KHRIMS DANG BRTUL ZHUGS DMAN PA LA CHAGS PA)

00:19:50.080 --> 00:20:01.640
There's a special wrong idea called
tsultrim dang tul shuk gyi tawa
(TSUL KHRIMS DANG BRTUL ZHUGS GYI LTA BA)--

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:06.320
attachment to wrong kinds of morality

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:21.360
and attachment to wrong kinds of asceticism,
like difficult spiritual practices.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:36.320
So tsultrim (TSUL KHRIMS), here I said "ethics,"
but I should say, I think, "a code of life."

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:48.960
And there is such a thing as a negative code of life, people commit to that negative code of life.

00:20:56.680 --> 00:21:01.160
There's a couple of examples in the ancient books.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:13.040
There used to be strict trades in India--your father's a butcher, you should be a butcher.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:27.800
And that person, when they reach a training time,

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:42.040
They'll make a commitment,
"I will follow the life of a butcher,"
"I will be a soldier."

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:45.360
That's one example.

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:47.920
The other is called tul shuk (BRTUL ZHUGS).

00:21:48.520 --> 00:21:57.720
These are difficult practices that are
supposed to be spiritual, but actually just hurt you.

00:22:06.360 --> 00:22:10.120
There were many many in India. One of them

00:22:12.480 --> 00:22:15.200
you hold your arm up

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:18.200
for two years.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:21.920
And if you can keep it up

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:29.160
then you're a good spiritual person, you can do something tough and hard,

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:33.040
and the arm doesn't get enough blood

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:40.040
and it shrinks, and after that you cannot use it.

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:45.160
Then they say, "Oh, he's very spiritual."

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:51.640
There are many religions where if you hurt yourself,

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:57.040
it's some special spiritual practice.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:05.360
So attraction to those
is the third kind of negative desire.

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:14.200
The fourth one,

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:18.040
dak tu mawa nyewar lenpa ni
(BDAG TU SMRA BA NYE BAR LEN PA NI)--

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:30.040
you are super attracted to saying,
"I am me," "Michael is Michael."

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:41.400
You could say "self-nature," but that's kind of confusing.

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:53.320
For example, is water wet? Can you say that water it wet?

00:23:54.400 --> 00:24:02.160
Sure. Can you walk on water?
No, not possible

00:24:02.640 --> 00:24:06.720
Why? Water is wet. You're going to to fall down.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:11.560
Then Buddhism, the deepest Buddhism,

00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:23.080
it says the wetness of water and the hotness of fire are not inside the water and they are not inside the fire.

00:24:31.320 --> 00:24:36.080
Your seeds put the hot in the fire.

00:24:39.080 --> 00:24:42.880
And your seeds put the wet in the water.

00:24:45.040 --> 00:24:49.400
And your seeds put the angry words
in your husband's mouth.

00:24:53.200 --> 00:24:57.280
And even what you hear in your own mind,

00:25:00.080 --> 00:25:04.440
what you hear when you listen to your own thoughts,

00:25:05.640 --> 00:25:08.760
those thoughts are also coming out of seeds,

00:25:09.920 --> 00:25:13.480
and the listener is coming out of seeds.

00:25:14.080 --> 00:25:16.840
So in a way,

00:25:18.040 --> 00:25:23.120
the husband in the kitchen is not my husband.

00:25:24.600 --> 00:25:31.520
"Why do you say that?"
I'm talking about the one where you say,
"I didn't do anything and he yelled at me."

00:25:33.680 --> 00:25:44.040
It's impossible for there to exist, in a billion years, any husband where the wife "didn't do anything."

00:25:52.960 --> 00:25:57.680
Because the husband is coming
from the seeds in the wife's mind.

00:26:02.120 --> 00:26:07.840
Now if we don't understand
why the husband is yelling at me,

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:12.760
if you don't understand
where the husband is coming from,

00:26:15.120 --> 00:26:21.600
then you will link two--you you will say,
"No, you're stupid," and you will make new karma.

00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:29.600
But if you understand who the husband really is--

00:26:33.200 --> 00:26:39.360
"This husband is yelling at me because I yelled at my kids last week; I put a seed in my mind."

00:26:42.520 --> 00:26:48.000
So the fourth kind of advanced desire here,

00:26:49.960 --> 00:26:56.400
link number nine, it refers to misunderstanding "me,"

00:26:58.120 --> 00:27:04.640
and "my" things, "my" husband, "my" house, "my" kids.

00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:17.160
And that's a good place to go to the higher school's understanding of these two links.

00:27:22.400 --> 00:27:33.480
What is it that makes the seed start to get fat under the ground, until it's ready to crack open?

00:27:40.720 --> 00:27:48.680
What's the real water and fertilizer--
which we can say is link eight and link nine,

00:27:53.080 --> 00:28:01.680
what's the real water and fertilizer that makes
a mental seed get ready to open?

00:28:05.440 --> 00:28:17.080
And don't forget that mental seed that we planted
in link number two is in the Wheel of Life,
and it's something bad.

00:28:23.760 --> 00:28:28.040
And in link number eight and link number nine
we are turning on the bomb.

00:28:31.040 --> 00:28:34.080
And it's going to explode.

00:28:34.080 --> 00:28:38.040
So you guys, if you came to the
Diamond Cutter Institute programs,

00:28:42.760 --> 00:28:45.680
or ACI programs,

00:28:46.120 --> 00:28:48.120
you studied le lam (LAS LAM),

00:28:50.040 --> 00:28:55.400
karma marga, you studied the four steps.

00:28:55.920 --> 00:28:57.920
So I ask you,

00:28:59.120 --> 00:29:04.040
how do you make a good seed grow faster and bigger?

00:29:07.400 --> 00:29:09.400
Tim?

00:29:11.440 --> 00:29:18.040
Coffee meditation! Thinking about your good seeds.

00:29:19.120 --> 00:29:22.320
Taking joy that you are doing good deeds.

00:29:24.160 --> 00:29:29.000
And understanding what you are doing

00:29:29.760 --> 00:29:33.000
during your coffee meditation.

00:29:33.800 --> 00:29:46.400
Those thoughts are like sunlight, they're like  water,
they are like fertilizer on the good seeds.

00:29:47.440 --> 00:29:53.400
So if there was a Wheel of Life for a good life

00:29:56.320 --> 00:30:01.880
Link number eight and link number nine
would be something like

00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:07.520
coffee meditation about the person
you helped this afternoon--

00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:18.680
--and don't forget during coffee meditation, you have two kinds of coffee meditation joined together:

00:30:21.960 --> 00:30:27.760
this one, "I'm so happy I helped somebody this afternoon,"

00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:35.240
and this one, "I'm so happy I have
a new way to make money," for example,

00:30:37.120 --> 00:30:41.000
which is helping the person this afternoon.

00:30:42.800 --> 00:30:45.880
"I'm happy I helped the person this afternoon.

00:30:47.040 --> 00:30:54.000
And I'm happy I have a new system where
helping other people is how I get money."

00:30:55.640 --> 00:31:02.760
So take those two and do a coffee meditation.

00:31:03.280 --> 00:31:09.400
That's how to make a good seed grow bigger and faster.

00:31:11.320 --> 00:31:16.800
Now, what's the real link eight? What's the real link nine?

00:31:18.920 --> 00:31:25.800
Because now we're talking about bad seeds.
And I will give you a new eight and nine.

00:31:29.320 --> 00:31:37.120
Number eight: did you kill a pig last week?

00:31:38.680 --> 00:31:41.800
"Yes." Are you sorry?

00:31:42.480 --> 00:31:44.120
"Nope!"

00:31:44.680 --> 00:31:48.280
Okay, that's like link number eight for a bad seed.

00:31:52.080 --> 00:31:55.840
It's like a negative coffee meditation.

00:31:56.520 --> 00:32:02.040
"Yeah, I'm glad I killed a pig. Now I got more protein.

00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:07.720
I'll be a stronger person." It is a completely stupid idea.

00:32:09.120 --> 00:32:14.560
Then what's a deeper kind of water and fertilizer?

00:32:16.040 --> 00:32:21.120
And this is where I wanted to take you
by the end of today, session 15.

00:32:26.080 --> 00:32:42.760
So listen: just understanding this system of the Wheel of Life is like sunlight on your good seeds.

00:32:43.160 --> 00:32:46.360
And the opposite of that:

00:32:48.160 --> 00:32:55.760
you don't study, you don't understand, you don't work hard to to see emptiness,

00:32:57.080 --> 00:33:00.040
you don't meditate every day,

00:33:01.120 --> 00:33:06.720
just that not understanding the system, and not doing it,

00:33:09.680 --> 00:33:11.680
that's the real link number nine.

00:33:12.800 --> 00:33:16.560
So if link number eight, for bad seeds,

00:33:18.120 --> 00:33:23.440
is to enjoy that you hurt somebody
and you don't feel bad,

00:33:25.920 --> 00:33:29.000
which is the half of a negative coffee meditation,

00:33:30.760 --> 00:33:36.080
then the more serious light on the bad seed

00:33:40.280 --> 00:33:45.400
is that you don't understand seeds at all.

00:33:48.080 --> 00:33:52.960
What's the real "advanced desire," link number nine?

00:33:55.520 --> 00:34:03.160
In the higher school, that seed is going to get fat and powerful and open faster

00:34:06.160 --> 00:34:11.080
if it has not sunlight, by radiation.

00:34:13.520 --> 00:34:22.080
Poison radiation coming from your mind:
"Ah, this seed stuff is stupid!"

00:34:23.560 --> 00:34:35.120
TThe pen is a pen." That thinking makes the
bad seeds grow faster and stronger.

00:34:37.440 --> 00:34:44.320
And those are the real link number eight
and link number nine for the "wheel of pain."

00:34:48.040 --> 00:34:56.000
"I'm not sorry I hurt someone.
He deserved it. He hurt me."

00:34:56.320 --> 00:35:01.680
"He called me 'stupid'.
I'm not sorry I called my husband 'stupid'."

00:35:02.720 --> 00:35:06.200
Well aren't you worried about planting bad seeds?

00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:12.160
"That's ridiculous!" Then you just did eight and nine.

00:35:13.080 --> 00:35:16.040
Okay, so let's be careful.

00:35:16.840 --> 00:35:23.800
Number one, don't yell at your husband,
even if he's stupid don't yell at him.

00:35:25.200 --> 00:35:27.800
Stay quiet, kill the seed.

00:35:29.120 --> 00:35:32.160
And link number nine,

00:35:32.400 --> 00:35:36.720
respect the seeds. Study more, and more, and more.

00:35:37.280 --> 00:35:40.880
Even if you can't stop fighting with your husband,

00:35:43.920 --> 00:35:47.000
keep learning more, and more, and more.

00:35:48.040 --> 00:35:56.640
And then there will be sunlight in your mind which makes these good seeds grow and the bad seeds stop.

00:36:03.440 --> 00:36:06.520
Okay, see you in session 16.

00:36:07.200 --> 00:36:11.200
We're going to talk about the fat seed.

00:36:12.720 --> 00:36:15.640
Thank you, and thanks for translating, Stanley.

